<p><strong>A barbershop booking app lets customers pick a barber and a time online, lets the shop fit in walk-ins around booked slots, and records each payment against the barber who did the work. Zennly provides this for single-chair shops and multi-branch barbershops in Nepal.</strong></p>
<p>Barbershops are the fastest-moving appointment business: short services, many customers and a mix of booked and walk-in trade. A paper list or a message thread cannot show which barber is free at 4:15 pm, which is why queues form and regulars walk out.</p>
<h2>What a barbershop actually needs</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Short, accurate slots.</strong> Service durations set once, so the diary fits itself.</li>
<li><strong>Walk-ins and bookings together.</strong> A walk-in takes a gap; it should not push out a booking.</li>
<li><strong>Barber-level records.</strong> Who did what, and how much each took.</li>
<li><strong>Simple payments.</strong> Cash, card and online recorded against each service. See <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Packages and loyalty</h2>
<p>Regulars often prefer a prepaid card or a set of visits. Track them with <a href="/features/memberships/">memberships</a> or <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a> instead of a notebook.</p>
<h2>More than one shop</h2>
<p>If you open a second shop, you need one view of both. Read the <a href="/blog/manage-multiple-spa-salon-branches-nepal/">multi-branch checklist</a>. For setup and pricing questions see <a href="/solutions/barbershop/">barbershop booking software</a>.</p>

<h2>A simple setup checklist for a barbershop</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>List your services and durations.</strong> Haircut, beard trim, shave and combinations each get a time, so the diary fills itself accurately.</li>
<li><strong>Add every barber.</strong> Give each barber their own schedule and breaks so clients can pick a person or just a time.</li>
<li><strong>Decide your walk-in rule.</strong> Keep a share of gaps open for walk-ins, and let staff add them in seconds.</li>
<li><strong>Record every payment.</strong> Note cash, card or online against the barber who did the work.</li>
<li><strong>Share one booking link.</strong> Put it on your Instagram, Facebook page and Google Business Profile so new customers can book at once.</li>
</ol>
<p>Weekends, festival eves and pre-wedding days are the peak. Open extra slots, make sure every barber's availability is correct, and check the day's totals before you lock up.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What booking app can a barbershop in Nepal use?</h3>
      <p>Zennly lets customers book a barber and time online, lets staff fit in walk-ins, and records payments for each barber.</p>
      <h3>Can a barbershop handle walk-ins and appointments together?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Walk-ins can be fitted into available gaps without disrupting booked appointments.</p>
      <h3>Can I see how much each barber earned?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Bookings and payments are recorded per staff member, so reports show revenue by barber.</p>
      <h3>Does a small barbershop need multi-branch features?</h3>
      <p>Not at first, but Zennly works for one chair or several branches, so you do not outgrow it.</p>
      
